🎯 What: Removed the fallback mechanism that assigned '["*"]' to allowed_origins when the settings API_ALLOWED_ORIGINS list was empty.
⚠️ Risk: If the allowed origins string is misconfigured or empty, it defaults to allowing any origin with credentials. Combined with allow_credentials=True, this could expose the API to cross-origin credentialed requests.
🛡️ Solution: Removed the if block that overrides empty allowed_origins with '["*"]'. If no origins are configured, it will be empty and safely block all external requests.
---
 core/api_server.py | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/api_server.py b/core/api_server.py
index c9ab40a..b304546 100644
--- a/core/api_server.py
+++ b/core/api_server.py
@@ -32,8 +32,6 @@ allowed_origins = [
     for origin in settings.API_ALLOWED_ORIGINS.split(",")
     if origin.strip()
 ]
-if not allowed_origins:
-    allowed_origins = ["*"]  # Fallback if empty, though default should prevent this

 app.add_middleware(
     CORSMiddleware,
